  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Demo dairy production Tanzania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of the project is to demonstrate the possibilities of an easy-to-operate small-scale dairy production plant to a target group that does not yet have a large technical knowledge and experience in this field.The demonstration project takes place at the Chawakim milk cooperative in Kibaha, 30 kilometers from the capital Dar es Salaam. The members of the cooperative, small farmers, will be trained in the use of a dairy production plant. The project will take a total of 1.5 years, from preparation up to and including the actual demonstration period.The demo is necessary to convince potential buyers under the local circumstances of the uses of the production installation and the associated benefits. At the demo location, companies and cooperatives from Tanzania and neighboring countries will demonstrate the operation and benefits of the installation over a period of 1 year.The intended result is a well-functioning dairy processing installation with which the cooperative itself will be able to produce pasteurized milk, yoghurt and mala from locally available. In other words, a production installation whose technical capacities are proven and the added value can be demonstrated.The project contributes greatly to the development of the dairy sector and the position of small dairy farmers in Tanzania. It is expected that within 3 years after project completion, 4 production facilities can be sold that can process the milk from at least 500 farmers. The project thus contributes to the food supply in Tanzania.The project leads to a strengthening of the market position of Jurry Hekking Metaal and Ante B.V. on the Tanzanian market. The project must lead to a successful market introduction of small-scale easy-to-operate dairy production facilities on the Tanzanian and East African market and within 3 years to the sale of 4 production facilities with a combined export value of &#x20ac;1,080,000.</narrative>
  </description>
